==== a `match` on one line has no line to add an arm on
---- file a.azl
fn main() {
    match true { true => print(1) }
}
---- run check --json a.azl
---- exit 1
---- stdout
{"severity":"error","code":"E0501","message":"this `match` does not handle `false`; add an arm for it or a final `_ =>` arm","file":"a.azl","line":2,"column":5,"end_line":2,"end_column":10,"source":"    match true { true => print(1) }","rule":"A `match` handles every case: each variant of an enum, both `true` and `false`, or has a final `_ =>` arm.","help":"Add the missing arms."}
{"summary":{"errors":1,"files":1}}
